---@field zone? string The zone in which to create the VM.
---@field metadata? gcp.vmmigration_v1.StringMap The metadata key/value pairs to assign to the VM.
---@field hostname? string The hostname to assign to the VM.
---@field diskReplicaZones? gcp.vmmigration_v1.StringList Optional. Additional replica zones of the target regional disks. If this list is not empty a regional disk will be created. The first supported zone would be the one stated in the zone field. The rest are taken from this list. Please refer to the [regional disk creation API](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/global-regional-zonal-resources) for further details about regional vs zonal disks. If not specified, a zonal disk will be created in the same zone the VM is created.
---@field appliedLicense? gcp.vmmigration_v1.AppliedLicense The OS license returned from the adaptation module report.
---@field bootOption? gcp.vmmigration_v1.ComputeEngineTargetDetailsBootOptionEnum|string The VM Boot Option, as set in the source VM.
---@field machineType? string The machine type to create the VM with.
---@field networkInterfaces? gcp.vmmigration_v1.NetworkInterfaceList List of NICs connected to this VM.
---@field licenseType? gcp.vmmigration_v1.ComputeEngineTargetDetailsLicenseTypeEnum|string The license type to use in OS adaptation.
---@field serviceAccount? string The service account to associate the VM with.
---@field labels? gcp.vmmigration_v1.StringMap A map of labels to associate with the VM.
---@field networkTags? gcp.vmmigration_v1.StringList A list of network tags to associate with the VM.
---@field diskType? gcp.vmmigration_v1.ComputeEngineTargetDetailsDiskTypeEnum|string The disk type to use in the VM.
---@field enableIntegrityMonitoring? boolean Optional. Defines whether the instance has integrity monitoring enabled.
---@field machineTypeSeries? string The machine type series to create the VM with.
---@field bootConversion? gcp.vmmigration_v1.ComputeEngineTargetDetailsBootConversionEnum|string Optional. By default the virtual machine will keep its existing boot option. Setting this property will trigger an internal process which will convert the virtual machine from using the existing boot option to another.
---@field vmName? string The name of the VM to create.
---@field storagePool? string Optional. The storage pool used for the VM disks. If specified this will be the storage pool in which the disk is created. This is the full path of the storage pool resource, for example: "projects/my-project/zones/us-central1-a/storagePools/my-storage-pool". The storage pool must be in the same project and zone as the target disks. The storage pool's type must match the disk type.
